PXL
----

Minimal 2D graphics library in C99.

Features:
  - 2D primitives: line, rect, circle, triangle (outline + filled)
  - Canvas with scissor clipping, color, clear, blit
  - ARGB8888 pixel buffer (pixbuf)
  - Backends: SDL2, X11
  - Keyboard/mouse input

Build:
  make          # lib + tests (SDL2 default)
  make test     # run tests
  make examples # all demos

  Backend selection via -DBACKEND_SDL / -DBACKEND_X11 flags.
  See examples/Makefile.

Example:
  See examples/demo.c for full API. Quick start:

    backend_init("Title", 800, 600, false);
    while (!input.quit_requested) {
        backend_poll_events(&input);
        backend_begin_frame(&pb);
        canvas_init(&cnv, &pb);
        /* drawing: draw2d_*(), canvas_*() */
        backend_end_frame();
    }
    backend_deinit();

Architecture:
  src/pixbuf.h        - ARGB8888 pixel buffer with stride alignment
  src/geom.h          - Geometry primitives (rect, span, point) and clipping
  src/canvas.h, c     - Drawing surface with color, scissor, clear, blit
  src/draw2d.h, c     - 2D primitives (line, rect, circle, triangle)
  src/backend.h       - Backend interface (5 functions)
  src/backend_sdl.c   - SDL2 backend (uses SDL_PIXELFORMAT_ARGB8888)
  src/backend_x11.c   - X11 backend (uses ARGB visual)
  include/err.h       - Error handling

